.TH se 7 "17 September 2016" "version 0.1.0"

.SH NAME
se - rapids storage engine

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B se [--start [--size n[b|kb|mb|gb|tb|pb] ] | --stop | --status] 

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B se
is a rapids storage engine.
 
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are available in this release:

.TP 
.B --start  
starts the storage engine. You can give an optional size of the shared memory. Default shared memory size is 4gb.
.TP
.RS
.RE
Example: se --start --size 8gb

.TP
.B --stop  
stops the storage engine

.TP
.B --status
displays the status of the storage engine

.TP
.B --prompt
starts se prompt

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B se --start
.RS
.RE
RapidsSE v0.1.1 (Sep 26 2016 11:33:56 -- debug)
.RE
Creating SE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1 ...
.RE
RapidsSE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1 started
.TP
.B se --status
.RS
.RE
RapidsSE v0.1.1 (Sep 26 2016 11:33:56 -- debug)
.RE
RapidsSE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1 running

.TP
.B se --stop
.RS
.RE
RapidsSE v0.1.1 (Sep 26 2016 11:33:56 -- debug)
.RE
Attaching to SE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1
.RE
RapidsSE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1 stopped

.TP
.B se --prompt
.RS
.RE
RapidsSE v0.1.1 (Sep 26 2016 11:33:56 -- debug)
.RE
Attaching to SE instance /RapidsSE_Instance1
.RE
se 0.1.1>
.TP
The commands that can be given to the se prompt are:

.RS
.RE
.B bye
-- exit out of the se prompt

.RE
.B cd <directoryName>
-- change directory to <directoryName>

.RE
.B cf <folderName>
-- change folder to <folderName>

.RE
.B create catalog <catalogName>;
-- create the catalog

.RE
.B create schema <schemaName>;
-- create the schema

.RE
.B create table <tableName>;
-- create the table

.RE
.B create tenant <tenantName>;
-- create the tenant

.RE
.B drop catalog <catalogName>;
-- drop the catalog

.RE
.B drop schema <schemaName>;
-- drop the schema

.RE
.B drop table <tableName>;
-- drop the table

.RE
.B drop tenant <tenantName>;
-- drop the tenant

.RE
.B lf
-- list folder contents

.RE
.B ld <tableName> <fileName>
-- load table

.RE
.B ex <tableName> <fileName>
-- export table into a file

.RE 
.B ls
-- list directory contents

.RE
.B lscol <tableName>
-- list columns of the table

.RE
.B print
print string

.RE
.B pwf
print working folder

.RE
.B pwd
print working directory

.RE
.B space
print the total, in use and free pool space

.RE
.B ?
print this help

.RE
.B help
print this help
